Sun Aug 30 15:34:04 UTC 2026 - Martin Pluskal <mpluskal@suse.com>

- Prepare the package for submission to openSUSE:Factory:
  * Rename the tarball to .tar.gz - it always was gzip, only the
    name claimed xz.
  * Drop the bogus /usr/lib RUNPATH from libdsdcc and dsdccx;
    upstream hardcodes it and the cmake macro only strips it on
    suse_version <= 1500.
  * Drop the Group tags, switch to autosetup and cmake_build, ship
    CHANGELOG, reword the descriptions.
  * Replace the libdsdcc.so.1* glob with the SONAME and the real
    library file, so a future libdsdcc.so.10 cannot be swallowed
    into libdsdcc1.
  * Record the licence audit above License, including
    descramble.cpp's embedded GPL-2.0-only notice from G4KLX.

